### Express Quota Guard Middleware

```javascript
function enforceHostSponsoredQuota(session, requestingUser, tokenCost, hostUser) {
  if (!session.shareConfig.linkActive && requestingUser.id !== session.ownerId) {
    throw new Error("Share link has been revoked by the Host.");
  }
  if (session.shareConfig.permission === "viewer" && requestingUser.id !== session.ownerId) {
    throw new Error("View-Only mode: Ask the Host to enable Collaborator prompting.");
  }
  if (session.shareConfig.tokensUsedInSession + tokenCost > session.shareConfig.tokenCap) {
    throw new Error("Session token cap reached. Host can raise the cap or you can Copy to Personal Account.");
  }
  // Deduct strictly from Host subscription pool
  hostUser.personalQuotaUsed += tokenCost;
  session.shareConfig.tokensUsedInSession += tokenCost;
}
```

Notice how **Hasnain's prompt** automatically billed **2,350 tokens** to **Robina Mirbahar's Host Pool**, while Hasnain's personal Enterprise quota remained untouched at `3,100 / 1,000,000`.
